        "old_string": "      \"worldUiCoupling\": \"world-ui reports coupling 0.58 from 9 imports targeting game-engine. This is structurally expected: world-ui is a leaf UI-composition zone whose sole purpose is to render engine state. The 9 imports break down as: 5 type/constant imports from the engine barrel (TileType, TILE_TYPE_DEFS, WorldData, LevelData, SVG_WIDTH/SVG_HEIGHT), 2 TilePreview component imports, and 2 hook imports (useWorldSession, useRainbowEasterEgg). All follow the correct DAG direction (UI → engine). The coupling score is below the warning threshold and the risk level is healthy. Reducing these imports would require either duplicating engine types in the UI layer or adding an unnecessary abstraction layer.\"",
        "new_string": "      \"worldUiCoupling\": \"world-ui reports coupling 0.58 from 9 imports targeting game-engine. This is structurally expected: world-ui is a leaf UI-composition zone whose sole purpose is to render engine state. The 9 imports break down as: 5 type/constant imports from the engine barrel (TileType, TILE_TYPE_DEFS, WorldData, LevelData, SVG_WIDTH/SVG_HEIGHT), 2 TilePreview component imports, and 2 hook imports (useWorldSession, useRainbowEasterEgg). All follow the correct DAG direction (UI → engine). The coupling score is below the warning threshold and the risk level is healthy. Reducing these imports would require either duplicating engine types in the UI layer or adding an unnecessary abstraction layer.\",\n      \"zoneBoundariesTestScope\": \"zone-boundaries.test.ts guards the entire 4-layer architecture DAG (engine → hooks → components → routes), making its conceptual scope global rather than zone-specific. It is classified in build-infrastructure because it is the runtime verification counterpart to eslint.config.ts — the static rule definition it validates. Both files form a cohesive pair: one defines the enforcement rules, the other proves they are correctly wired. This is not a misclassification; architecture enforcement tooling belongs with the build infrastructure that implements it.\""
